==Production and budget==

===KTK and the pillarized system===

The Taisen drama is produced by [[KHR]] (Kokumin Hōsō Renmei, "National Broadcasting Alliance"), the oldest and largest of the seven broadcasting associations within [[KTK]]'s pillarized system. KHR represents the Imperial establishment, traditional Sanese culture, and conservative social values, and has approximately 12.4 million paid members as of 2025. The Taisen drama is KHR's flagship production, occupying the prestigious Sunday 20:00 slot on KTK:1 and receiving the largest single share of KHR's annual production budget.

KTK's funding model — a combination of 0.05% of Okaiken's Value Added Tax, membership fees collected by each broadcasting association, and commercial sponsorship on designated programming — means that the Taisen drama's budget is directly tied to KHR's membership revenue. KHR's 28% airtime share on KTK:1, the largest of any association, reflects its dominant membership base and ensures that the Taisen drama receives priority scheduling and resource allocation.

The pillarized structure creates a unique production environment. Unlike a centralized broadcaster where a single programming department controls all content, KHR's editorial apparatus operates independently within its own "pillar" — a structure that the 2026 ''Hatsu'' controversy exposed as a potential blind spot, as decisions to alter historically significant content can be made within a single pillar's editorial apparatus without visibility to the cross-pillar coordination structure or the Broadcasting Council.

===Budget evolution===

