The 2026 series ''Hatsu: Shiokaze no Kōgō'' set a new budget record at ¥3.8 billion, driven by the construction of three full-scale warship replicas and the use of 400 extras for the Siege of Sai River arc. The series also marked the first time a Taisen drama's budget exceeded that of a major Sanese theatrical film.

===Content Standards Guidelines===

Following the 1962 ''Akō Rōshi'' beheading controversy, KTK established its first Content Standards Guidelines in 1963, codifying rules for the depiction of violence on Sanese television. The guidelines have been revised multiple times — most notably in 1969 (to accommodate colour broadcasting), 1984 (to address the increasing intensity of battle sequences), and 2000 (to address HD-level graphic detail). The 2026 ''Hatsu'' controversy has prompted calls for the first comprehensive review since 2000, with the Diet Communications Committee considering whether the guidelines should be updated to address not only the depiction of violence but the suppression of historically significant content.


==Cultural significance==

The Taisen drama occupies a unique position in Sanese cultural life, blending the bloodier, more visceral strands of the ''[[jidaigeki]]'' tradition with the serialized storytelling of the modern television era. Unlike the more restrained Onnamono dramas, which tend to emphasize court intrigue and personal relationships, the Taisen drama is defined by its unflinching depiction of warfare — battlefield tactics, political assassinations, and the human cost of ambition. This emphasis on martial realism has roots in the ''Kassen Manga'' tradition of illustrated battle stories, which flourished in the postwar years after the Shaydian occupation lifted and the Sanese public reconnected with its martial heritage through the restoration of castles such as Suemori in Nagayama Prefecture and Matsushiro in Kōchi Prefecture.

The genre has also been instrumental in shaping public understanding of Okaiken's geography. For many viewers, the Taisen drama is their first introduction to the three-island structure of the archipelago — campaigns that range across the volcanic highlands of Ishijima, the great plains of Yagikoshu, and the mountainous interior of Harujima. Filming on location at restored castles and historical sites across all 48 prefectures has made the series a de facto visual tour of the nation's heritage, and local governments frequently compete for the economic boost that comes with being selected as a filming location.

==Technological milestones==

The Taisen drama has been a consistent driver of broadcasting technology innovation in Okaiken, often serving as the first production to adopt new formats and techniques:

